WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm great.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.703
-Welcome back.
You went down to McAllen, Texas.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
And I was very glad --

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
You weren't the only one
who went,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I have a lot of respect
for people who went down there

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
to actually see what
it was like on the ground.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your biggest takeaway
from what we had been told

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
about a place
like McAllen, Texas,

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.282 size:78% position:39%
and what it was like
actually being there?

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
the two biggest ones --

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first is this idea
that this is chaos

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're being overrun
is preposterous.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.088 line:92%
I mean, people were just like,

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you even
talking about?" down there.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.059
It's like, "This is life, yeah.
We live in McAllen.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
Reynosa, Mexico,
is across the border.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.230 line:92%
And, you know, people come in,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
they go back
for years and decades

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.433 size:88% position:44%
and, actually, centuries
in American life, right?

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
This has been
a part of the country

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.569
where people move back and forth
across that river.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
The idea that there is
some crazy invasion happening

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
was just entirely preposterous
and absent

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.846
from everyone I talked to there,
so that was the first thing.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
The second thing
was just the level

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.050 line:92%
of both courage and desperation

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the people
showing up at that border.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.886 line:92%
I mean, the stories you hear --

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.789
"The cartels come, and they
tried to recruit my oldest son,

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he said no,
and they shot and killed him.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:58.858 line:92%
So, now I have my youngest son,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I took him on a 2,000-mile
journey to come up here

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come to your door, America,
and be like,

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:07.100
'Please, take me in because
I don't want to give the cartels

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.501 line:92%
my only other living son.'"

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those are the kinds of stories
you're hearing

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.739
when you're watching the
President and other people

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his allies
talk about these people

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
like they're vermin
who's infesting the country.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:16.976 line:92%
You're talking about, literally,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.879
some of the most courageous
people in the hemisphere.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It is --

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:26.319
I mean, that's why I'm so happy
that people went down.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
Melania Trump
also went down there.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:29.756 line:92%
To her credit. To go down.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.625
With that said, Donald Trump,
he went to Duluth, Minnesota.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you're just gonna
move right past the jacket.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.664
-I mean, I don't even know
what to make of the jacket.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.900
The jacket -- The amount of
"did she know, did she not?"

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I feel like
it's something, you know --

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.905 size:78% position:39%
-She's going to get a
face tattoo that says
"I hate all of you."

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone's gonna be like,
"Oh, what does it mean?
I don't know."

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's like a Magic 8-Ball
that doesn't have a die in it.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you just shake it,
and it's just black water.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:59.652
So, that -- I mean, I'm like,
I guess we could keep trying,

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.588
but I don't think we're
ever gonna get an answer.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She went down there. Yeah.
-She went down there.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.692 size:75% position:38%
Donald Trump went to
Duluth, Minnesota,

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
to rage about
the immigration party --

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
the immigration problem,
I should say.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.931 line:92%
-It was the most perfect moment

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
that encapsulated
what this is really about.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.702
We're down in McAllen. We're
talking to folks in McAllen.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're talking to --
A guy I talked to,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
had a conversation with --
20 years in CBP,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.341 line:92%
you know, border protection.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.009 line:92%
I talked to lawyers for migrants

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people that offer them,
you know, care.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're talking about,
"What a situation."

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile,
he flies north to Duluth

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.818
and, in a huge stadium of folks
all keyed up in Duluth,

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
is talking about
the scourge at the border.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.722 size:81% position:41%
And we're down at the
border like, "What are
you talking about?"

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.857
But that's the whole point.
He did this on the campaign.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.426
You know, he would go to Kenosha
or he'd go to somewhere in Ohio

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.029
and talk about the border,
and people would be chanting,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:43.997 line:92%
like, going nuts about it.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it's not
actually the border.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
It's this idea of invasion.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's this idea
of the country's changing

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:50.970 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in ways they don't like.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.008
The border is a convenient
metaphor for that anxiety.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.209 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Obviously, immigration

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been framed as a problem
for a really long time.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it safe to say
that the real issue

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.116
is that there are certain people
that don't see it

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.285
as an immigration problem
but as a diversity problem?

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:08.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-More than that.
An existential problem
about what the country is.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.790
I mean, Stephen Miller
is very clear about this.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steven King,
the Iowa Congressman

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:15.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
who tweeted literal
Nazi propaganda a week ago.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are people
that really think

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the nature of the country
existentially --

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.634 size:88% position:44% line:92%
America won't be America

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it changes too much
demographically.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.604 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And they see themselves

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
as guarding against
that eventuality,

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're very clear
about that.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's why it's very hard
to come to compromise

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
with these people
about legislation.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, even when you go
and you say,

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.381 size:81% position:41%
"We're gonna put money
into border security,"

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:36.216 line:92%
which we've done every year.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.483 size:84% position:42%
Border-security numbers
are through the roof.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.952
"We're going to have more people
patrolling the border."

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:41.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which we've done every year.
There's more people
patrolling the border.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
They say, "Okay.
Now let's strike a deal."

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they say,
"No, we don't want a deal.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.359 line:92%
Because what we want to do

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
is change the demographic tide
of this country

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
to preserve the white majority
we have now."

